B18 - Contribute to an open-source cybersecurity project

Objective
The goal of this activity is to contribute to an open-source project related to cybersecurity and understand secure development practices.

Method
I reviewed an open-source GitHub project and contributed improvements related to documentation, security awareness, and project organisation.

Findings
1. Improved project documentation to better explain secure usage practices.
2. Identified areas where sensitive information should not be publicly exposed in repositories.
3. Added recommendations for safer handling of credentials and configuration files.

Security Principle
This activity reinforced:
- Secure software development practices
- Protection of sensitive information
- Community collaboration in cybersecurity
- Security awareness in development environments

Evidence
- Screenshot of the GitHub repository homepage
- Screenshot of commit history or contribution made
- Screenshot of edited README/documentation changes
- Notes describing the contribution and security improvements added

Reflection
This activity showed how open-source collaboration can improve cybersecurity awareness and project quality. Even small improvements such as documentation updates and security recommendations can help reduce risks in software projects.
